New Orleans Daily Picayune.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:03.100
Eventually, Jim Crow conquered New Orleans as well.

00:33:05.300 --> 00:33:11.360
In 1890, the Louisiana legislature decreed that blacks and whites must occupy different

00:33:11.360 --> 00:33:14.120
cars on trains traveling within the state.

00:33:16.400 --> 00:33:22.870
Two years later, a New Orleans Creole of color named Homer Adolph Plessy set out to

00:33:22.870 --> 00:33:28.310
test the new law, boarding an excursion train and insisting on sitting in the whites only

00:33:28.310 --> 00:33:28.710
car.

00:33:30.700 --> 00:33:33.410
He was arrested, tried, and convicted.

00:33:35.580 --> 00:33:39.170
In 1896, in the case of Plessy v. Ferguson,

00:33:40.070 --> 00:33:43.530
the Supreme Court of the United States upheld his conviction.

00:33:45.200 --> 00:33:48.370
Separate but equal facilities, it said, were constitutional.

00:33:50.560 --> 00:33:53.480
That decision would govern life in the American South

00:33:53.480 --> 00:33:57.240
and in New Orleans for nearly 60 years.

00:33:59.030 --> 00:33:59.970
City theaters and...

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:06.590
restaurants were now strictly segregated. Black and white boxers and bicycle racers

00:34:06.590 --> 00:34:13.320
and baseball teams were forbidden to compete against one another. The state legislature

00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:21.670
then passed a law barring all would-be voters whose grandfathers had been slaves. Where 95%

00:34:21.670 --> 00:34:28.580
of the city's black men had been registered to vote, just 1% was now eligible to go to the polls.

00:34:31.850 --> 00:34:34.670
And the world of the Creoles was turned upside down, too.

00:34:36.430 --> 00:34:40.400
By law, they now found themselves classified with blacks

00:34:40.400 --> 00:34:42.670
as second-class citizens.

00:34:42.990 --> 00:34:49.440
And all these Creole people suddenly became black people overnight.

00:34:51.550 --> 00:34:54.590
And these Creole orchestras, which existed at one point,

00:34:54.900 --> 00:34:55.860
suddenly disappeared.

00:34:56.160 --> 00:34:58.610
And these clarinetists had no work.

00:34:59.140 --> 00:34:59.980
So they were essentially...

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:08.650
forced to go into the black community and that level of technical fluency forever

00:35:08.650 --> 00:35:14.390
changed the nature of the music. Creole musicians merged their classical

00:35:14.390 --> 00:35:21.400
virtuosity with the blues-inflected music of black bands. Together they would

00:35:21.400 --> 00:35:24.440
transform every kind of music played in New Orleans.

00:35:31.150 --> 00:35:34.890
had a strict kind of beat, and they were often slow,

00:35:36.560 --> 00:35:38.580
and they said exactly what they meant,

00:35:38.760 --> 00:35:40.480
and they meant exactly what they said.

00:35:41.350 --> 00:35:48.400
And the musicians sometimes had to fill in space,

00:35:49.360 --> 00:35:51.510
one phrase to the next one,

00:35:53.650 --> 00:35:57.230
