01:15:47.560 --> 01:15:52.290
But in this particular instance, in this nation, it is race.

01:16:04.960 --> 01:16:12.070
Shortly after midnight on January 1st, 1913, the New Orleans police made an arrest.

01:16:14.620 --> 01:16:20.050
An 11-year-old boy had been caught firing his stepfather's .38 revolver into the air

01:16:20.050 --> 01:16:22.680
in celebration of the new year.

01:16:24.740 --> 01:16:26.320
He was not unknown to the police.

01:16:27.670 --> 01:16:29.970
And the next morning, a judge sentencing...

01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:33.200
to an indeterminate term in the colored waif's home.

01:16:36.070 --> 01:16:38.570
His name in the neighborhood was Little Louie,

01:16:40.620 --> 01:16:43.110
but his full name was Louis Armstrong,

01:16:43.310 --> 01:16:49.110
and he would one day transform American music.

01:17:02.110 --> 01:17:03.510
Next time on Jazz.

01:17:03.770 --> 01:17:05.070
Good evening, ladies and gentlemen.

01:17:06.390 --> 01:17:07.470
I'm Armstrong.

01:17:07.990 --> 01:17:09.750
You talk about Louis Armstrong, well.

01:17:10.030 --> 01:17:12.510
You're talking about the deepest human feeling

01:17:12.510 --> 01:17:15.090
and the highest level of musical sophistication.

01:17:18.700 --> 01:17:21.560
Armstrong's great contribution is impossible to notate,

01:17:21.960 --> 01:17:25.560
but it is the characteristic that most clearly defines jazz.

01:17:26.180 --> 01:17:26.740
Swing.

01:17:31.200 --> 01:17:43.780
I believe Louis Armstrong was a real human being.

01:17:44.130 --> 01:17:46.750
God sent him to this earth to be a special messenger.

01:17:47.020 --> 01:17:49.960
And the result is so overpowering and so spiritual,

01:17:51.430 --> 01:17:53.230
it's enough to make the angels weep.

